# KS-1087 — Wednesday's task for Ornith, ITEM 1 ONLY (written from the ticket AND the code at develop M55 `48e65c435`, 2026-09-15 09:5x)

## What is wrong (one paragraph)
In `services/api-gateway/src/routes/verification.ts`, the approve handler of `POST /api/workflow-instances/:id/approve`
forwards the pending document to originate with `http.request`, then — without waiting for or reading originate's
response — deletes the pending document from Redis (line 991, `await redisService.deletePendingDocument(documentId)`)
and answers 200 `approved` (lines 994–1002). If originate answers 401 (it does today) or is unreachable, the
document is lost and the caller is told it was created. **Only item 1 of the ticket is in scope: report approval and
delete the pending document ONLY after originate returns 2xx; on any other status or a network error, keep the
pending document and return an error.** Item 2 (which credential originate accepts) is a design decision — do NOT
change `forwardHeaders` or add any header.

## The exact change — the block at lines 975–1002 (inside `if (pendingDoc) { … }`), one site
Today the request is fire-and-forget: the `proxyRes.on('end')` callback only logs (line 983), the `error` handler
only logs (line 987), and lines 991 + 994 run unconditionally. Rewrite ONLY this block so that:
1. The forward is awaited: wrap `http.request(...)` in a `Promise<{ status: number }>` that resolves with
   `proxyRes.statusCode` on `'end'` and REJECTS on the `'error'` event (keep the two existing `log(...)` calls
   where they are, inside the callbacks).
2. After awaiting it: if the status is 2xx (`status >= 200 && status < 300`) → `await redisService.deletePendingDocument(documentId)` and fall through to the existing 200 `res.json({... status: 'approved' ...})` (lines 994–1002, unchanged).
3. Otherwise (a non-2xx status, or the promise rejected) → do NOT delete the pending document; respond
   `res.status(502).json({ success: false, error: { code: 'ORIGINATE_FORWARD_FAILED', message: 'Approved, but the document could not be created in originate; the pending document was kept', status: <the status or 0> } })` and `return;`.
Keep `payload`, `forwardHeaders`, `originateUrl`, `url` exactly as they are (lines 959–974). Do not touch the
reject handler (line 1006 onward) or anything above line 955. No new imports.

## The test — one new vitest file, in-process, no server
File: `services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1087-workflow-approve-keeps-doc-on-originate-failure.test.ts`
Copy the mocking shape from `services/api-gateway/src/__tests__/ks1071-verify-confidence-one-mapping.test.ts`
(it imports `../routes/verification` and stubs its dependencies in-process). Stub `redisService` so
`getWorkflowInstance` returns an instance whose last step is being approved (read how the handler reaches the
`if (pendingDoc)` branch above line 955 and satisfy exactly that), `getPendingDocument` returns a document, and
`deletePendingDocument` is a `vi.fn()`. Stand up a real local `http` server on port 0 as the originate stub
(`services.originate.url` pointed at it) that answers a status you choose per cell. Cells:
- 🔴 `it('🔴 KS-1087 — originate 401: no 200 approved, and the pending document survives')`: stub answers 401;
  assert the response status is not 200 (expect 502) and `deletePendingDocument` was NOT called. (Untouched
  code: 200 and the delete is called — the red.)
- 🔴 `it('🔴 KS-1087 — originate unreachable: the pending document survives')`: point the URL at a closed port;
  same assertions.
- CONTROL `it('KS-1087 control — originate 201: approved and the pending document is deleted')`: stub answers
  201; assert 200 `approved` and `deletePendingDocument` called once — before and after.
Close the stub server in `afterEach`.

